EF AI Workspace (#218): MCP servers for admins only, owner decision 2026-10-25 («فعلها للمسؤول بس»; ADR-0021).
The role permissions are set before every start by infrastructure/common/roles-policy.js (ADMIN use and add, nobody
shares); upstream already shows the MCP page only to a role that may add servers or that has a server to use.

- «More» (UnifiedSidebar/efSidebar.ts, EfMoreMenu.tsx): the MCP page joins the admin tools under «Admins only» with
  the «Admins» badge, named «MCP servers» (com_ui_mcp_servers), and opens in the panel beside the rail as the builder.
- Links (hooks/Nav/useUnifiedSidebarLinks.ts): employees never get the admin panels (EF_ADMIN_PANELS), so a temporary
  role-editor grant does not put the MCP page in the employees' sidebar.
- Panel header (UnifiedSidebar/EfChatsPanel.tsx): the way back reads «‹ Chats» (accessible name «Back to chats»), so a
  tool's name is no longer clipped in 300 px («MCP servers» read «MCP…», «Agent builder» too).
- Tests: ExpandedPanel.spec (the MCP page in the admin group, with the badge, opened in the panel).

